#
# description : This .audit is designed against the CIS Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG Benchmark v1.0.0
#
#<ui_metadata>
#<display_name>CIS Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG v1.0.0 CAT I</display_name>
#<spec>
#  <type>CIS</type>
#  <name>Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG</name>
#  <profile>CAT I</profile>
#  <version>1.0.0</version>
#  <link>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698</link>
#</spec>
#<labels>agent,cis,windows_iis_10</labels>
#<benchmark_refs>800-53,800-53r5,CAT,CCI,LEVEL,Rule-ID,STIG-ID,Vuln-ID</benchmark_refs>
#<variables>
#  <variable>
#    <name>PLATFORM_VERSION</name>
#    <default>(10|20[12][269])</default>
#    <description>Windows Platform Version</description>
#    <info>Windows Platform Version</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#  <variable>
#    <name>PRODUCT_VERSION</name>
#    <default>10\.0</default>
#    <description>IIS Product Version</description>
#    <info>IIS Product Version</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#</variables>
#</ui_metadata>

<check_type:"Windows" version:"2">
<group_policy:"CIS Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "Verify IIS is installed."
      value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data  : "(internet|iis)"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\W3SVC"
      reg_item    : "ImagePath"
      check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "Verify IIS 10 installed."
      value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data  : "^Version @PRODUCT_VERSION@[\s]*$"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Inetstp"
      reg_item    : "VersionString"
      check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "Windows Server 2016/2019/2022 and Windows 10"
      value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data  : "^[a-zA-Z0-9\(\)\s]*@PLATFORM_VERSION@[a-zA-Z0-9\(\)\s]*$"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows Nt\Currentversion"
      reg_item    : "ProductName"
      check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "CIS_Microsoft_IIS_10.0_Site_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_I.audit from CIS Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG v1.0.0"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
          description : "Check if anonymous authentication is enabled for any IIS site."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "true"
          appcmd_args : "list config {} /section:system.webserver/security/authentication/anonymousAuthentication /text:enabled"
          appcmd_list : "list sites"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <if>
          <condition auto:"WARNING" type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
              description : "Verify the anonymous authentication username is restricted (not a broad group account)."
              value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data  : "^Manual Review Required$"
              appcmd_args : "list config {} /section:system.webserver/security/authentication/anonymousAuthentication /text:userName"
              appcmd_list : "list sites"
              severity    : MEDIUM
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
              description     : "Verify the anonymous access account is not a member of a privileged group."
              value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data      : "^Manual Review Required$"
              powershell_args : "Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_Group | Select-Object Name"
              severity        : MEDIUM
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.14 IIST-SI-000221"
              info        : "Anonymous IIS 10.0 website access accounts must be restricted.

GROUP ID: V-218750
RULE ID: SV-218750r961095

Many of the security problems that occur are not the result of a user gaining access to files or data for which the user does not have permissions, but rather users are assigned incorrect permissions to unauthorized data. The files, directories, and data stored on the web server must be evaluated and a determination made concerning authorized access to information and programs on the server. Only authorized users and administrative accounts will be allowed on the host server in order to maintain the web server, applications, and review the server operations.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
              solution    : "Remove the Anonymous access account from all privileged accounts and all privileged groups."
              reference   : "800-171|3.13.3,800-53|SC-2,800-53r5|SC-2,CAT|I,CCI|CCI-001082,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-2,ITSG-33|SC-2a.,LEVEL|1M,NESA|T3.4.1,NIAv2|SS15b,Rule-ID|SV-218750r961095_rule,STIG-ID|IIST-SI-000221,Vuln-ID|V-218750"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.14 IIST-SI-000221"
          info        : "Anonymous IIS 10.0 website access accounts must be restricted.

GROUP ID: V-218750
RULE ID: SV-218750r961095

Many of the security problems that occur are not the result of a user gaining access to files or data for which the user does not have permissions, but rather users are assigned incorrect permissions to unauthorized data. The files, directories, and data stored on the web server must be evaluated and a determination made concerning authorized access to information and programs on the server. Only authorized users and administrative accounts will be allowed on the host server in order to maintain the web server, applications, and review the server operations."
          solution    : "Remove the Anonymous access account from all privileged accounts and all privileged groups."
          reference   : "800-171|3.13.3,800-53|SC-2,800-53r5|SC-2,CAT|I,CCI|CCI-001082,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-2,ITSG-33|SC-2a.,LEVEL|1M,NESA|T3.4.1,NIAv2|SS15b,Rule-ID|SV-218750r961095_rule,STIG-ID|IIST-SI-000221,Vuln-ID|V-218750"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
        </report>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"OR">
        <custom_item>
          type        : REG_CHECK
          description : "Verify WSUS server role is installed (registry)."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Update Services\Server\Setup"
          reg_option  : MUST_EXIST
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "Verify WSUS server role is installed (service present, any state)."
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : ".*WSUSInstalled.*"
          powershell_args : "if (Get-Service -Name 'WsusService' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) {'WSUSInstalled'} else {'NotInstalled'}"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
          description : "Verify SharePoint is installed"
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "sharepoint"
          appcmd_args : "list site /state:Started /text:name"
          check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : REG_CHECK
          description : "Verify OCSP Responder service is installed."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\OCSPSvc"
          reg_option  : MUST_EXIST
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : REG_CHECK
          description : "Verify NDES (Network Device Enrollment Service) is installed."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\Mscep"
          reg_option  : MUST_EXIST
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : REG_CHECK
          description : "Verify CRL distribution service (CertSvc / AD CS) is installed."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\CertSvc"
          reg_option  : MUST_EXIST
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.33 IIST-SI-000242"
          info        : "The IIS 10.0 private website must employ cryptographic mechanisms (TLS) and require client certificates.

GROUP ID: V-218768
RULE ID: SV-218768r1111814

TLS encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2-approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.

NIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems."
          solution    : 'Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:

Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.

Double-click the \'SSL Settings\' icon under the \'IIS\' section.

Select the \'Require SSL\' setting.

Select the \'Client Certificates Required\' setting.

Click \'Apply\' in the \'Actions\' pane.

Click the site under review.

Select \'Configuration Editor\' under the \'Management\' section.

From the \'Section:\' drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \'system.webServer/security/access\'.

Click on the drop-down list for \'sslFlags\'.

Select the \'Ssl128\' check box.

Click \'Apply\' in the \'Actions\' pane.'
          reference   : "800-171|3.13.16,800-171r3|03.13.08,800-53|SC-28(1),800-53r5|SC-28(1),CAT|I,CCI|CCI-002476,CN-L3|8.1.4.7(b),CN-L3|8.1.4.8(b),CSF|PR.DS-1,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,GDPR|32.1.a,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iv),HIPAA|164.312(e)(2)(ii),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ITSG-33|SC-28(1),LEVEL|1M,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|3.4,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.3.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-218768r1111814_rule,STIG-ID|IIST-SI-000242,TBA-FIISB|28.1,Vuln-ID|V-218768"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>

      <else>
        <if>
          <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type                : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
              description         : "Verify Require SSL is enabled for HTTPS-bound sites"
              value_type          : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data          : '(^| )Ssl(,|$)'
              appcmd_args         : 'list config {} /section:access /text:sslFlags'
              appcmd_filter       : 'list sites {} /text:bindings'
              appcmd_filter_value : 'https'
              appcmd_list         : 'list sites'
              check_type          : CHECK_REGEX
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type                : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
              description         : "Verify client certificates are required for HTTPS-bound sites"
              value_type          : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data          : '(^| )SslRequireCert(,|$)'
              appcmd_args         : 'list config {} /section:access /text:sslFlags'
              appcmd_filter       : 'list sites {} /text:bindings'
              appcmd_filter_value : 'https'
              appcmd_list         : 'list sites'
              check_type          : CHECK_REGEX
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type                : AUDIT_IIS_APPCMD
              description         : "Verify 128-bit SSL encryption is enforced for HTTPS-bound sites"
              value_type          : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data          : '(^| )Ssl128(,|$)'
              appcmd_args         : 'list config {} /section:access /text:sslFlags'
              appcmd_filter       : 'list sites {} /text:bindings'
              appcmd_filter_value : 'https'
              appcmd_list         : 'list sites'
              check_type          : CHECK_REGEX
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.33 IIST-SI-000242"
              info        : "The IIS 10.0 private website must employ cryptographic mechanisms (TLS) and require client certificates.

GROUP ID: V-218768
RULE ID: SV-218768r1111814

TLS encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2-approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.

NIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems."
              solution    : 'Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:

Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.

Double-click the \'SSL Settings\' icon under the \'IIS\' section.

Select the \'Require SSL\' setting.

Select the \'Client Certificates Required\' setting.

Click \'Apply\' in the \'Actions\' pane.

Click the site under review.

Select \'Configuration Editor\' under the \'Management\' section.

From the \'Section:\' drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \'system.webServer/security/access\'.

Click on the drop-down list for \'sslFlags\'.

Select the \'Ssl128\' check box.

Click \'Apply\' in the \'Actions\' pane.'
              reference   : "800-171|3.13.16,800-171r3|03.13.08,800-53|SC-28(1),800-53r5|SC-28(1),CAT|I,CCI|CCI-002476,CN-L3|8.1.4.7(b),CN-L3|8.1.4.8(b),CSF|PR.DS-1,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,GDPR|32.1.a,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iv),HIPAA|164.312(e)(2)(ii),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ITSG-33|SC-28(1),LEVEL|1M,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|3.4,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.3.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-218768r1111814_rule,STIG-ID|IIST-SI-000242,TBA-FIISB|28.1,Vuln-ID|V-218768"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </else>
    </if>
  </then>

  <else>
    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "CIS_Microsoft_IIS_10.0_Site_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_I.audit from CIS Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site STIG v1.0.0"
      info        : "NOTE: Nessus has not identified that the chosen audit applies to the target device."
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23698"
      show_output : YES
    </report>
  </else>
</if>

</group_policy>
</check_type>
